{"source_sha256":"7f3917fffb205a0e09f80145bc8bd78c982ad9a6fef18d9d84b64b9d4b5ece8e","page_number":32,"page_type":"text-native","blocks":[{"id":"a-cairn-warden-32-b1","text":"Page 32","bbox":[27.0,587.64,52.02,597.34]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-32-b2","text":"Dungeon Seeds","bbox":[27.0,42.84,173.56,70.54]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-32-b3","text":"Dungeon Principles","bbox":[27.0,79.65,140.23,96.27]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-32-b4","text":"Purpose Consider what the dungeon’s original purpose was as well as what it is being used for today. Demonstrate a dungeon’s history by including signs of its original inhabitants and their goals. Sometimes a dungeon will have multiple purposes, and these can collide against each other to create tension among its denizens.","bbox":[27.0,102.88,345.21,160.19]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-32-b5","text":"Levels Though they should make sense as part of the dungeon’s construction and purpose, levels should also represent increasing danger. On each level, try to push players to weigh the risk of further exploration versus a potential reward.","bbox":[27.0,167.88,340.13,214.19]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-32-b6","text":"Layout Create multiple entrances and exits, offer multiple routes, design choke points, and provide hiding spots. Add meaningful and obvious information to room entrances and exits.","bbox":[27.0,221.88,347.3,268.19]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-32-b7","text":"Verticality Incorporate tall rooms, climbable structures, and paths that allow movement around and over obstacles.","bbox":[27.0,275.88,343.6,311.19]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-32-b8","text":"Secret Areas Include hidden zones, including at least one that will likely remain undiscovered but is still worth finding. Try to avoid hiding crucial information behind secret rooms.","bbox":[27.0,318.88,349.47,354.19]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-32-b9","text":"Rooms Vary room shapes, sizes, and functions. Use architectural motifs to connect rooms and provide hints of what’s to come. Room descriptions should be easy to map and recall.","bbox":[27.0,361.88,351.26,397.19]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-32-b10","text":"Treasure Incorporate a variety of treasures beyond mere gold, such as knowledge, allies, trade goods, and artifacts. Add narrative elements to treasure to increase its non-monetary value.","bbox":[27.0,404.88,346.9,451.19]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-32-b11","text":"Challenges Allow the characters to drive the story by writing challenges without prescribed outcomes. Create a sense of peril, but avoid making obstacles seem unbeatable. Overly dangerous areas and creatures should be obvious. Create encounters that can be avoided with critical thinking and problem-solving, not just violence. Remember that monsters and other obstacles are another way to tell the dungeon’s story.","bbox":[27.0,458.88,350.9,527.19]}],"reading_order":["a-cairn-warden-32-b2","a-cairn-warden-32-b3","a-cairn-warden-32-b4","a-cairn-warden-32-b5","a-cairn-warden-32-b6","a-cairn-warden-32-b7","a-cairn-warden-32-b8","a-cairn-warden-32-b9","a-cairn-warden-32-b10","a-cairn-warden-32-b11","a-cairn-warden-32-b1"],"headings":[{"id":"h-cairn-warden-32-1","anchor":{"text":"Dungeon Seeds","bbox":[27.0,42.839874267578125,173.55999755859375,70.53987121582031]},"level":1},{"id":"h-cairn-warden-32-2","anchor":{"text":"Dungeon Principles","bbox":[27.0,79.65202331542969,140.23202514648438,96.27201843261719]},"level":2,"parent_id":"h-cairn-warden-32-1"},{"id":"h-cairn-warden-32-3","anchor":{"text":"Purpose","bbox":[27.0,102.87989807128906,66.2699966430664,116.72989654541016]},"level":3,"parent_id":"h-cairn-warden-32-2"},{"id":"h-cairn-warden-32-4","anchor":{"text":"Levels","bbox":[27.0,167.87989807128906,57.150001525878906,181.7299041748047]},"level":3,"parent_id":"h-cairn-warden-32-2"},{"id":"h-cairn-warden-32-5","anchor":{"text":"Layout","bbox":[27.0,221.87989807128906,59.76000213623047,235.7299041748047]},"level":3,"parent_id":"h-cairn-warden-32-2"},{"id":"h-cairn-warden-32-6","anchor":{"text":"Verticality","bbox":[27.0,275.8798828125,78.11000061035156,289.7298889160156]},"level":3,"parent_id":"h-cairn-warden-32-2"},{"id":"h-cairn-warden-32-7","anchor":{"text":"Secret Areas","bbox":[27.0,318.8798828125,87.43000030517578,332.7298889160156]},"level":3,"parent_id":"h-cairn-warden-32-2"},{"id":"h-cairn-warden-32-8","anchor":{"text":"Rooms","bbox":[27.0,361.8798828125,59.230003356933594,375.7298889160156]},"level":3,"parent_id":"h-cairn-warden-32-2"},{"id":"h-cairn-warden-32-9","anchor":{"text":"Treasure","bbox":[27.0,404.8798828125,70.1300048828125,418.7298889160156]},"level":3,"parent_id":"h-cairn-warden-32-2"},{"id":"h-cairn-warden-32-10","anchor":{"text":"Challenges","bbox":[27.0,458.8798828125,79.11000061035156,472.7298889160156]},"level":3,"parent_id":"h-cairn-warden-32-2"}],"section_continuations":[{"id":"sc-cairn-warden-32-to-33","source":{"page_number":32,"block_id":"a-cairn-warden-32-b11"},"destination":{"page_number":33,"block_id":"a-cairn-warden-33-b2"},"section_relation":"SAME_SECTION","content_continuity":"NONE"},{"id":"cairn-warden-31-to-32-different-section","source":{"page_number":31,"anchor":{"text":"Worldbuilding: Put It All Together","bbox":[256.4,14.4,369.0,24.1]}},"destination":{"page_number":32,"block_id":"a-cairn-warden-32-b2"},"section_relation":"DIFFERENT_SECTION","content_continuity":"NONE"},{"id":"cairn-warden-118-to-119-unresolved","source":{"page_number":118,"anchor":{"text":"Adjectives","bbox":[27.0,43.704,86.076,60.324]}},"destination":{"page_number":119,"anchor":{"text":"Nouns","bbox":[45.0,43.704,81.936,60.324]}},"section_relation":"UNRESOLVED","content_continuity":"NONE"}]}
{"source_sha256":"7f3917fffb205a0e09f80145bc8bd78c982ad9a6fef18d9d84b64b9d4b5ece8e","page_number":33,"page_type":"text-native","blocks":[{"id":"a-cairn-warden-33-b1","text":"Page 33","bbox":[343.84,587.64,369.0,597.34]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-33-b2","text":"NPCs Include engaging NPCs with their own goals and agendas. These characters may want to stay in the dungeon; they may even love it! NPCs and monsters should communicate with the PCs, even during combat. Have them make threats, suggest compromises, or try to persuade the PCs whenever possible. Every character wants something, and has a limit to what they might do to get it.","bbox":[45.0,43.92,370.7,112.23]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-33-b3","text":"Factions Factions should interact with both the characters and one another, acting on their own regardless of the character’s actions. Give them hierarchies and divisions that can be exploited.","bbox":[45.0,119.92,368.86,166.23]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-33-b4","text":"Puzzles Create puzzles that have clear, actionable goals. Puzzles should reinforce the themes of the dungeon and build on its history. Make the challenge of the puzzle obvious, but the solution less so. Allow for multiple solutions, and for players to solve them using intelligence and critical thinking, not just special abilities or tools. Create built-in clues suggesting the puzzle’s origin and its effects.","bbox":[45.0,173.92,369.55,242.23]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-33-b5","text":"The Dungeon Map Put boring or repetitive stuff (exits, room shapes, etc.) on the map, rather than in the room description. Obvious exits should be described using clear, distinct language. Number your rooms to help avoid confusion when referencing the map.","bbox":[45.0,249.92,361.76,296.23]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-33-b6","text":"Room Keying Emphasize a room’s most important aspects (typically obvious threats or NPCs). Describe elements that help orient the party to their surroundings. Be specific, but avoid describing how the characters should feel. Only describe what’s happening now. If there is history here, the characters will discover it in play. Name each room!","bbox":[45.0,303.92,367.28,361.23]},{"id":"a-cairn-warden-33-b7","text":"Encounter Tables Create random events to help make a dungeon feel alive by making exploration tense and unpredictable, as parties may encounter wandering monsters, factions, NPCs, or signs of an approaching threat. Try to provide challenges, moments of respite, or opportunities for roleplay.","bbox":[45.0,368.92,362.92,426.23]}],"reading_order":["a-cairn-warden-33-b2","a-cairn-warden-33-b3","a-cairn-warden-33-b4","a-cairn-warden-33-b5","a-cairn-warden-33-b6","a-cairn-warden-33-b7","a-cairn-warden-33-b1"],"headings":[{"id":"h-cairn-warden-33-1","anchor":{"text":"NPCs","bbox":[45.0,43.91987609863281,70.8499984741211,57.769874572753906]},"level":3},{"id":"h-cairn-warden-33-2","anchor":{"text":"Factions","bbox":[45.0,119.91999816894531,85.4000015258789,133.77000427246094]},"level":3},{"id":"h-cairn-warden-33-3","anchor":{"text":"Puzzles","bbox":[45.0,173.9199981689453,81.19999694824219,187.77000427246094]},"level":3},{"id":"h-cairn-warden-33-4","anchor":{"text":"The Dungeon Map","bbox":[45.0,249.9199981689453,132.4199981689453,263.7699890136719]},"level":3},{"id":"h-cairn-warden-33-5","anchor":{"text":"Room Keying","bbox":[45.0,303.91998291015625,108.2199935913086,317.7699890136719]},"level":3},{"id":"h-cairn-warden-33-6","anchor":{"text":"Encounter Tables","bbox":[45.0,368.91998291015625,128.74000549316406,382.7699890136719]},"level":3}]}
